## What ran

The [frozen question](QUESTION.md) converts authored legacy inputs with independent
positive object-presence variables into the existing deletion-audit representation.
It preserves every possible object set, matching graph and paired loss.
Unconditional object presence becomes an explicitly hypothetical derived premise,
bound to the original authored case. It is not a new observation or a human label.

All512small graph/presence cases agree with complete independent enumeration of
1,728original worlds. All six larger cases agree with the conventional calculation.
Ten unsupported-input controls refuse conversion. Sixteen mutations of actual
stored results are rejected, including lost context, forged matching witnesses,
empirical promotion and confusing audit insufficiency with detector inferiority.
The checker runs with the engine's endpoint producer and matching-proposal
entry point disabled. Shared authorship, parser and runtime remain limitations.

