## Use and limits

Use the existing revision-audit interface when its declared model applies:
`audit --proof-method monotone`. Read the
[existing method and its admission rules](../../perception-revision/0.1.0/README.md#ordered-reference-endpoints-for-preserved-base-additions).
This does not permit arbitrary detector replacement or reinterpretation of
real evidence as hypothetical measurements.

The new conversion remains a research example limited to authored synthetic
inputs. It rejects shared variables, clauses, negative/conjunctive conditions,
conditional edges, missing/open data and non-synthetic material. Do not extend
the guard to more complex models without a new checked semantic argument.

Reproduce with the existing qualified Python environment containing NumPy2.4.2,
SciPy1.17.1 and jsonschema; install nothing in this mission:

```sh
python -B research/presence-endpoints/0.1.0/run.py /tmp/reiyah-presence-FRESH.json
python -B research/presence-endpoints/0.1.0/check.py \
